{"id": "EUVD-2026-59731", "enisaUuid": "d74db22c-653c-395f-83d2-8ad95b3ac3d8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: lock sk in iso_connect_ind\n\nAccessing iso_pi(sk)->conn requires lock_sock, which is not taken in the\n\"ev3\" part of iso_connect_ind.  It may also be NULL if socket has\ntransitioned away from the LISTEN/CONNECT states before locking.\n\nFix by adding lock/release. Recheck hcon is valid after lock acquire\nwhere needed.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:51", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e830354c120954ccb9ca15880245912722c4031", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8e9cff6d80eeec28dec4cf7cc18662986945391", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9bee7e476534f27e830658dad962d85da9edf6bf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4311fd6f429065a8ba208660360a895627a00cf3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hqwp-mg54-6754", "CVE-2026-74538"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f54056d-1c85-34fe-bfa3-109c6f311373", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "2004a456-bc6a-3de9-beed-2223bc0d415b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "21e07da0-38c5-31f9-b25d-8b5c57a6a83d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "168d9bf9c7f01df71e6404cfff66d9c2a8e968fb <9bee7e476534f27e830658dad962d85da9edf6bf"}, {"id": "3e3a96e9-7b67-3613-8bd0-4b6d96736eb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "486a16ac-0bb6-3f92-aeac-c0a38e4dafb7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "168d9bf9c7f01df71e6404cfff66d9c2a8e968fb <e8e9cff6d80eeec28dec4cf7cc18662986945391"}, {"id": "5bb3a5a6-25d4-38b5-80e